{{also|checkout}}
==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|sg=to [[check]] [[out]]|checks out|checking out|checked out}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[pay]] the [[bill]], and [[record]] one's [[departure]], as from a [[hotel]].
#: ''Be sure to '''check out''' before noon.''
# {{intransitive}} To [[leave]] in a [[hurry]].
# {{intransitive|euphemism}} (''by extension'') To [[die]].
# {{intransitive}} To have one's [[purchase]]s recorded and [[bagged]] at a [[supermarket]], and pay for it.
# {{transitive}} To [[withdraw]] an [[item]], as from a [[library]], and have the withdrawal recorded.
# {{transitive}} To [[examine]] or [[inspect]]; to [[espy]].
# {{transitive}} To obtain computer [[source code]] from a [[repository]].
# {{idiom|slang|as imperative}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to draw attention to something and stimulate excitement about it.}}
#: '''''Check''' it '''out'''! Best prices in town.''
#: '''''Check''' ''this'' '''out'''! They just arrested the Mayor!''
#: ''When you're there, '''check out''' the Cheddar Cheese Museum! It's a hoot!''

